ed on september  23rd as part of bnsf's regular  inspection program former ntsb chairman  robert sumwalt says the tracks will be  just one area of focus in the  investigation so if you were on the  ground here what would you be looking  for they'll be looking at three primary  things they'll be looking at the  operation of the train  was the locomotive engineer properly  controlling the train what is the  condition of the track is there anything  about the track itself that could have  led to a derailment and finally the  mechanical condition of the train was  there anything with the train that could  have led to a  derailment ntsb says once they determine  what caused this accident they are  committed to taking action to prevent  anything similar in the future somewhat  also tells me investigators will be  looking at what led to the injuries and  fatalities and whether seat belts could  have prevented them nate  meg thank you
 

